        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://bioportal.bioontology.org/ontologies/STMSO#Symptom"/>
        <rdfs:label>Uhthoff phenomenon</rdfs:label>
        <STMSO1:definition>Uhthoff phenomenon, also known as Uhthoff sign or Uhthoff syndrome, is a transient worsening of neurological function lasting less than 24 hours that can occur in multiple sclerosis patients due to increases in core body temperature.
(https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/books/NBK470244/)</STMSO1:definition>
    </owl:Class>
    


